### =====================================================================
### customer-service - ready-to-run requests
###
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### Calls the service DIRECTLY on port 8102, so we send the X-User-* headers
### ourselves (normally the API gateway adds them from the JWT).
###
### Seed data (docs/seed-data.md):
###   customer 1 = user 4 Priya Sharma   addresses 1 (HOME, default) and 2 (WORK)
###   customer 2 = user 7 Rahul Verma    address 3 (HOME, default)
###   customer 3 = user 9 Anita Desai    no addresses
### New customers get a profile automatically from the UserRegistered event.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8102


### 1. CUSTOMER (user 4): my profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 2. CUSTOMER (user 4): update my profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "fullName": "Priya Sharma",
  "phone": "9000000004",
  "dateOfBirth": "1994-05-17",
  "gender": "FEMALE"
}


### 3. CUSTOMER (user 4): my addresses
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me/addresses
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 4. CUSTOMER (user 9): first address -> automatically the default ("setAsDefault" is optional)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me/addresses
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 9
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "label": "HOME",
  "contactName": "Anita Desai",
  "contactPhone": "9000000009",
  "addressLine1": "7, Brigade Road",
  "landmark": "Opposite Bata Showroom",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "state": "Karnataka",
  "pincode": "560025"
}


### 5. CUSTOMER (user 4): add a third address and make it the default
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me/addresses
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "label": "OTHER",
  "contactName": "Meera Sharma (mother)",
  "contactPhone": "9845098450",
  "addressLine1": "45, 3rd Cross, Jayanagar 4th Block",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "state": "Karnataka",
  "pincode": "560011",
  "setAsDefault": true
}


### 6. CUSTOMER (user 4): make the WORK address (id 2) the default
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me/addresses/2/default
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 7. CUSTOMER (user 4): update the HOME address (id 1)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me/addresses/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "label": "HOME",
  "contactName": "Priya Sharma",
  "contactPhone": "9000000004",
  "addressLine1": "Flat 302, Lakeview Apartments",
  "addressLine2": "2nd Main Road, HAL 2nd Stage",
  "landmark": "Near Indiranagar Metro, Gate 2",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "state": "Karnataka",
  "pincode": "560038"
}


### 8. CUSTOMER (user 7): someone else's address (id 1 belongs to user 4) -> 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me/addresses/1
X-User-Id: 7
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER


### 9. CUSTOMER: invalid address -> 400 with one error per field
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me/addresses
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "label": "HOME",
  "contactName": "",
  "contactPhone": "12345",
  "addressLine1": "x",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "state": "Karnataka",
  "pincode": "5600"
}


### 10. ADMIN: search customers by name, email or phone
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/customers?keyword=sharma
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 11. ADMIN: one customer and their addresses
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/customers/1/addresses
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 12. INTERNAL (service-to-service): address 3 of user 7 - used by order-service at checkout
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/customers/7/addresses/3


### 13. No profile for this user (e.g. a vendor) -> 404 with a helpful message
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/customers/me
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
